<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Friedrich Joachim Stengel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1694">1694</a>–<a href="/years/1787">1787</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Friedrich Joachim Stengel (1694–1787) was a German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> architect who served the princes of Nassau-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saarbrucken">Saarbrücken</a> as their master builder. He shaped Saarbrücken as a Baroque residence, designing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ludwigskirche">Ludwigskirche</a>, the palace and the Ludwigsplatz ensemble, as well as churches, palaces and town plans across the Saar region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/friedrich-joachim-stengel.jpg" alt="Friedrich Joachim Stengel" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Friedrich-Joachim_Stengel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
